WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(lively jazzy music)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.476
- [Narrator] Welcome
to Rochester, New York.

00:00:02.476 --> 00:00:03.747
The home of Kodak Eastman,

00:00:03.747 --> 00:00:04.580
(camera clicks)

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:05.807
situated on Lake Ontario,

00:00:05.807 --> 00:00:08.080
and creator of the finest delicacy

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:09.054
in all the land.

00:00:09.054 --> 00:00:09.887
(phone rings)

00:00:09.887 --> 00:00:10.720
- [On Phone] Hey, can I have a plate

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.270
with all the garbage on it, please?

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:14.962
- [Narrator] That my
friends is the Garbage Plate

00:00:14.962 --> 00:00:16.728
and let me tell you,

00:00:16.728 --> 00:00:17.978
it is glorious.

00:00:22.382 --> 00:00:24.299
- My name is Alex Tahou.

00:00:24.299 --> 00:00:26.325
My grandfather invented
the original Garbage Plate,

00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:27.668
called Hots and Potatoes,

00:00:27.668 --> 00:00:29.949
and my father perfected
the real Garbage Plate.

00:00:29.949 --> 00:00:31.157
- [Narrator] At this point,
you're probably wondering,

00:00:31.157 --> 00:00:33.101
what this so-called Garbage Plate is.

00:00:33.101 --> 00:00:34.012
And I'll tell you.

00:00:34.012 --> 00:00:35.678
A garbage plate is--

00:00:35.678 --> 00:00:37.757
- Let me handle this.

00:00:37.757 --> 00:00:39.840
The Garbage Plate starts
with your choice of sides,

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.866
from home fries, french fries,

00:00:41.866 --> 00:00:43.754
macaroni salad or beans.

00:00:43.754 --> 00:00:45.263
Then you pick your meat,

00:00:45.263 --> 00:00:46.630
hot dogs, hamburgers, cheeseburgers,

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:48.113
whatever's on the menu.

00:00:48.113 --> 00:00:49.328
Then you add your toppings,

00:00:49.328 --> 00:00:50.929
from mustard, onions and hot sauce,

00:00:50.929 --> 00:00:52.788
ketchup and Red Hot is optional.

00:00:52.788 --> 00:00:54.639
Then add two pieces of
Italian bread and butter,

00:00:54.639 --> 00:00:56.056
and you're all set to go.

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:57.882
Over the years, we've had a lot

00:00:57.882 --> 00:00:59.046
of different kind of Garbage Plates.

00:00:59.046 --> 00:01:01.333
We actually had our
sardine plate years ago.

00:01:01.333 --> 00:01:03.338
I don't think you can get
much crazier than sardines.

00:01:03.338 --> 00:01:07.137
(sizzling)
(enchanting music)

00:01:07.137 --> 00:01:09.438
The best part of this business
is, of course, the customers.

00:01:09.438 --> 00:01:11.000
Without them, we'd be nothing.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.699
The place was established
to give people a lot of food

00:01:13.699 --> 00:01:15.336
at a reasonable price.

00:01:15.336 --> 00:01:17.256
For years people have come in here hungry

00:01:17.256 --> 00:01:18.459
and didn't have any money.

00:01:18.459 --> 00:01:19.793
My father always fed them.

00:01:19.793 --> 00:01:20.626
- [Narrator] That's really sweet Alex,

00:01:20.626 --> 00:01:21.992
but let's get back to the garbage,

00:01:21.992 --> 00:01:23.440
because I'm really wondering,

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:25.132
how many calories are in a plate?

00:01:25.132 --> 00:01:26.178
- [Alex] I really don't know.

00:01:26.178 --> 00:01:27.732
Some people have said 3,000.

00:01:27.732 --> 00:01:28.669
I don't think it's that high,

00:01:28.669 --> 00:01:32.197
but I guess I'd have to be
a nutritionalist to tell ya.

00:01:32.197 --> 00:01:33.784
But I will say this is the only place

00:01:33.784 --> 00:01:34.897
you can get a Garbage Plate.

00:01:34.897 --> 00:01:36.955
Any other plate in Rochester is a copycat.

00:01:36.955 --> 00:01:40.563
We trademarked it, so
now, it's world famous.

00:01:40.563 --> 00:01:42.468
- [Narrator] Trademarking garbage?

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:43.301
Genius.

00:01:46.185 --> 00:01:48.935
(digital jingle)

